chx:Research a res:ResearchProject ; rdfs:label "Functions for an advanced course: chapter 4 of the 3rd edition and today's Python"@en ;
    sen0414:methodology "Primary source first: the chapter's named concepts from the textbook ontology built over the published chapter. Then the official documentation for the current release and the PEPs the chapter's topics touch. Every source opened and read on 2026-09-28T23:09:18; every claim taken from text actually read; every behaviour executed under Python 3.14.4. Added in 1.1.0: sources P17 to P31, each fetched and read on 2026-10-01 (19:39:44 to 19:39:50), read for the definitions of the terms the chapter text used without defining them; every output and error message quoted in the corpus was executed under Python 3.12.11 and 3.14.4, and under 3.10, 3.11 and 3.13 where a sentence names those releases." ;
    res:hasResearchScope chx:Scope ; rdfs:member chx:P01, chx:P02, chx:P03, chx:P04, chx:P05, chx:P06, chx:P07, chx:P08, chx:P09, chx:P10, chx:P11, chx:P12, chx:P13, chx:P14, chx:P15, chx:P16, chx:P17, chx:P18, chx:P19, chx:P20, chx:P21, chx:P22, chx:P23, chx:P24, chx:P25, chx:P26, chx:P27, chx:P28, chx:P29, chx:P30, chx:P31 .
chx:Scope a res:ResearchScope ; res:hasResearchQuestion "What does chapter 4 of the 3rd edition teach about defining and calling functions, return values, the call stack, variable scope and exception handling, which of its printed outputs still hold under Python 3.14.4, and what must an advanced course add so that it matches current Python?" ; res:hasTimeWindow "Current as of 2026-10-01." .
